      "message": "\u003e In recent versions of CMake (perhaps since `add_compile_definitions` was introduced), `add_definitions` when called with an argument that starts with `-D` just forwards to `add_compile_definitions`, so there would be no change in behavior.  Additionally, `add_compile_definitions` was only added in cmake 3.12 so we would need to bump the minimum version number --- if that sounds fine then I can go ahead.  It is only problematic to use `add_definitions` for compiler options that are not `-D`.\n\nThanks for the the info. I didn\u0027t look closely enough what version that was added. I\u0027d like to keep compatibility while we can:\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/webm/libwebp/+/3929753",
